      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm putting together a 10-year outlook for some real estate holdings in the metro area. I've got access to some census and demographic trend data for the different districts. Based on historical trends, how much weight should I be giving to shifting racial and ethnic compositions when predicting whether a neighborhood will remain stable vs. seeing a decline in property values/desirability? Is demographic homogeneity generally a better indicator of long-term value retention?",
