    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "makes sense. to be more specific tho, if i'm looking at two comparable neighborhoods—same school ratings and similar median income—but one is becoming more diverse while the other is staying mostly white, which one is the \"safer\" bet for long-term appreciation? i'm trying to minimize risk from potential social friction or shifts in neighborhood character that usually come with rapid demographic changes.",
