      "content": "i see. so basically you're saying that diversity itself is a risk factor for investment stability. if we look at the data, is it fair to say that when a neighborhood transitions from majority white to a more diverse makeup, it's a leading indicator that property values will eventually stagnate or even drop? i just want to make sure i'm not missing the direct correlation between demographic shifts and the eventual decline of a neighborhood's status.",
